  "caveats": [
    "Streaming budget limits each sub-window to <= 7 CT chunks (~0.02-0.04 cm2); results are per-window aggregates, not whole-strip coverage.",
    "Sub-windows are chosen from mesh geometry only (fewest chunks / max curvature); presence of a dark seam in a window is measured afterwards (ct_dark_px_frac_below_half_median), never used for selection.",
    "clean_papyrus_retention_frac counts BOTH void halo and mesh-border erosion halo; void_halo_frac and void_detection_fired isolate the dark-void rule.",
    "Rendered pixels with zero CT intensity (masked-out air) are invalid, so fully empty gaps appear as border halo; the void rule can only fire on partial-volume dark seams.",
    "The physical rule is fixed a priori (dark_frac_of_median = 0.5: majority-air under linear partial-volume mixing); sweeps are reported, never used to tune."
  ],
